# Radial residues modulo 31
# Squared distance folded by a prime forms repeating targets and curved bands.

:mim 1

# The signed lattice keeps the origin at the visual center.
:axis x integers
:axis y integers

# x² + y² is squared distance; modulo 31 folds it into repeating radial bands.
:field mod(x * x + y * y, 31)

# Preserve the remainder and map its magnitude to a continuous paint scale.
:lens value
:color magnitude(lens)

# The diagonal is unrelated to this radial instrument.
:overlay equality off
